@format 1
@id section-naming.inline-editor-open
@title Open inline section-name editor
@section Section naming
@area In Split tab
@entry row-double-click
@summary Select a Split section and replace its row name display with the inline main-name/prefix/suffix editor when the row is double-clicked.
@related section-naming.inline-editor-input, section-naming.pending-inline-commit, section-naming.switch-inline-edit-target
@tag section
@tag split
@tag name
@tag rename
@tag inline-editor

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias history = Cadroue.Application.LHistory

[row-double-click] Section row MouseLeftButtonDown <input>
~ This starts when the user presses a section row.
[Technical explanation]
- The row's double-click handler is entered only for ClickCount at least two; PreviewMouseLeftButtonDown does not start drag capture for that double-click @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...) / row MouseLeftButtonDown
> click-check

[click-check] Double-click accepted <decision>
~ The program checks whether the row press is a double-click.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionRowBuild tests ClickCount and sends values below two to the ignored branch while an accepted double-click continues toward inline editing @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...) / row MouseLeftButtonDown
? "ClickCount below two" > ignored
? "Double click" > clear-drag

[ignored] Inline rename not requested <output>
~ This path ends with inline rename not requested.
[Technical explanation]
= Single-click selection/drag handling is outside this map.

[clear-drag] Clear row-drag state <process>
~ This step handles clear row-drag state.
[Technical explanation]
- Release row-panel mouse capture and clear tracked drag state before resolving the rename target @ panel.PSectionDragClear(...)
> index-check

[index-check] Current row index valid <decision>
~ The program checks current row index valid.
[Technical explanation]
- Resolve the row's current Children index and return if it is negative @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...) / rename-index resolution
? "Index invalid" > gone
? "Index valid" > select-flow

[gone] Rename target disappeared <output>
~ This path ends with rename target disappeared.
[Technical explanation]
= No editor opens.

[select-flow] Select section before editing <process>
~ This step handles select section before editing.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionSelect delegates the target index to LSegmentSelect @ flow.PFlowSectionSelect(...)
> segment-select

[segment-select] Publish selected section <process>
~ The program announces which section is now selected.
[Technical explanation]
- LSegmentSelect updates the active index and synchronously invokes LSegmentChange @ segment.LSegmentSelect(...)
> selection-observers

[selection-observers] Update Split selection observers <process>
~ This step handles update Split selection observers.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSegmentHandle updates Viewfinder/Map selection and invokes PFlowSectionChange, then the Sections panel reacts and Workspace history sees selection change before inline editing is enabled @ flow.PFlowSegmentHandle(...)
@ workspace.PWorkspaceSectionHandle(...)
@ history.LHistoryAdd(...)
> install-editor

[install-editor] Install inline editor for selected row <process>
~ This step handles install inline editor for selected row.
[Technical explanation]
- Store pSectionIndexEditing and rebuild the panel; PSectionEditorBuild replaces that row's display name with TextBoxes for LPieceName, LPiecePrefix, and LPieceSuffix @ panel.PSectionRebuild(...)
@ panel.PSectionEditorBuild(...)
> focus-name

[focus-name] Focus and select main name <output>
~ This path ends with focus and select main name.
[Technical explanation]
- On Loaded, the main-name box receives focus and SelectAll; existing non-empty affixes start visible while empty affix fields start collapsed @ panel.PSectionEditorBuild(...)
